#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0258 expect=violation domain=CO
#note "FLIPPED noViolation -> violation by Fix #331 (M3-D18 / M2-D24 bucket 1, owner ruling 2026-08-22): NonEmptyGuardInliner's bare-emptiness arm is RETIRED (Fix #330), so the machine-emitted var_exists guard this scenario used to pin no longer exists; absent = all-missing, empty(X) is TRUE on every row and the rule reports the defect on exactly the rows its other conjuncts select (1 here). If this goes SILENT again, a guard is being injected -- escalate, do not rewrite toward silence. History, before Fix #330: THE INJECTED-GUARD TRIPWIRE. There is deliberately NO IDVAR column. Under the corpus's absent-column doctrine (absent column = all-missing column) this row satisfies the sheet's Rule cell and SHOULD look violating -- but the shipped Check carries `var_exists(\"IDVAR\") and empty(IDVAR)`, machine-emitted by NonEmptyGuardInliner's bare-emptiness arm, so the conjunct is FALSE and the rule stays silent. If the guard-injection contract is ever changed or the arm removed, this scenario flips red and names the reason. ESCALATE if it FIRES on the first run -- do not 'fix' it toward the observed behaviour."
#library standard=sendig version=3-0
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset CO
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col POOLID   type=Char label="Pool Identifier"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col COSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col COVAL    type=Char label="Comment"
---
S1 | CO |  |  |  |  | 1 | Orphan comment
---
